      "description": "Two principal stones as two SEPARATE Stone Instances, DELEGATED the same way, each with its own scale and its own gem identity. PARTIAL for TWO reasons, and both are recorded rather than approximated: the non-primary stone is not held, exactly as for the cluster; and the two stones cannot differ in CUT, because a FamilyMember is an occurrence of the design's one `stone` and carries no shape (FAMILY-GOV). An oval-and-pear pair therefore needs per-member stone specifications, which is an existing Sprint 24 RFC."
